From b3677fc3d68dd942c92de52f0bd9dd8b472a40e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Amadeusz=20S=C5=82awi=C5=84ski?= <amadeuszx.slawinski@linux.intel.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2020 16:47:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: topology: Check return value of pcm_new_ver
Mime-version: 1.0
Content-type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-transfer-encoding: 8bit
Git-commit: b3677fc3d68dd942c92de52f0bd9dd8b472a40e6
Patch-mainline: v5.7-rc3
References: bsc#1051510

[ backport note: add declaration of ret for addressing the build error ]

Function pcm_new_ver can fail, so we should check it's return value and
handle possible error.

Signed-off-by: Amadeusz Sławiński <amadeuszx.slawinski@linux.intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Ranjani Sridharan <ranjani.sridharan@linux.intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20200327204729.397-6-amadeuszx.slawinski@linux.intel.com
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/soc/soc-topology.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sound/soc/soc-topology.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-topology.c
@@ -1902,6 +1902,7 @@ static int soc_tplg_pcm_elems_load(struc
 	struct snd_soc_tplg_pcm *pcm, *_pcm;
 	int count = hdr->count;
 	int i;
+	int ret;
 	bool abi_match;
 
 	if (tplg->pass != SOC_TPLG_PASS_PCM_DAI)
@@ -1935,7 +1936,9 @@ static int soc_tplg_pcm_elems_load(struc
 			_pcm = pcm;
 		} else {
 			abi_match = false;
-			pcm_new_ver(tplg, pcm, &_pcm);
+			ret = pcm_new_ver(tplg, pcm, &_pcm);
+			if (ret < 0)
+				return ret;
 		}
 
 		/* create the FE DAIs and DAI links */
